Z||000000||84sleepr||12-08-2001||05:07 PM||||OK, I have a slight question/ concern about by baby.  The other day I opened the oil fill<BR>cap and the inside was covered with a white, kinda frothy coating.  My best guess is that some moisture got in there.  Would that be a good assumption and if so what's the best way to get rid of it?<P>The car was sitting for a few years before a got it.  I've been giving it oil changes almost weekly to try to get rid of it.  Is there some sort of addiditive to add to the oil to get rid of this 'condition'???<P>Thanks in advance||||reg||5
