Z||000008||Ferrari_cdn||12-08-2001||09:40 PM||||  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Mach10:<BR><B> [QUOTE]Originally posted by Shinerdc:<BR>[b]maybe if i ever get my 84 running....a long weekend cruise for a tims would be a good idea....is the offer open to all?</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><BR>From Ontario!?!? If you're willing to make the haul, we'd be happy to see you...    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"> Why the HELL would you wanna visit Winnipeg? <P>[/B][/QUOTE]<P>So he can do donuts or figure 8s on our parking lots?    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>And the majority of the people in our group owns an 84, so he would fit in well.    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>Actually, Shinerdc, we're usually at Tim's for like 1 or 2 hours and then go home.  A long weekend drive for a 2 hour chat?  Maybe add a few more things on that list to do, and then it'll be more of a reason to come.  Racing the ricers (we have an insane number of ricers, but they wouldn't know that one of us has 400 horsies  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_brow.gif"> ), doing a cruise, a barbecue, and that would be a good weekend.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>If you meant to visit us in something like January or February, then bring warm clothing.  Winnipeg's cold weather is a ***** .<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/ICEFierosig.gif">  AIM: CanadianFiero<p>[This message has been edited by Ferrari_cdn (edited 12-08-2001).]||||reg||7
Z||000009||fiero56||12-09-2001||11:07 AM||||As long as the oil is still looking good in the crankcase, I wouldn't be too worried. Every winter, my Formula has white foam under the oil fill cap. It has been doing this for the past 50K miles. My oil always looks good, my coolant always looks good, exhaust is always clear, coolant and oil never really change their levels. <P>I figure it is probably a plugged PCV, or tube something not allowing the crankcase to breathe as it should. I've never bothered to look into it, never any problems so far. And this is with 184K miles on a totally stock 2.8L.||||reg||1
Z||000010||DRH||12-09-2001||11:24 AM||||I agree with Fiero56. If it's just in the valve cover and the oil looks OK when you drain it I don't think you have a serious problem. Changing the PCV might help. If you only take short trips, it might not be getting hot enough to get rid of all the moisture, you might want to take it for a nice trip.||||reg||1
